# tflint Custom Rule Standards

## When to Write Custom Rules
Write custom tflint rules when built-in rules don't enforce:
- Workspace-specific naming conventions
- Mandatory variable patterns (e.g., always include `common.variables.tf`)
- Deprecated resource type bans
- Organization-specific resource argument requirements

For simple value checks, prefer checkov YAML policies. Use tflint Go rules for structural/AST-level checks.

## Plugin Layout

```
tflint-ruleset-{{COMPANY_SLUG}}/
  rules/
    {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_naming_convention.go
    {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_naming_convention_test.go
    {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_required_tags.go
    {{COMPANY_SLUG}}_required_tags_test.go
  main.go
  go.mod
  go.sum
```

## Rule Boilerplate

```go
package rules

import (
    "github.com/terraform-linters/tflint-plugin-sdk/hclext"
    "github.com/terraform-linters/tflint-plugin-sdk/tflint"
)

type {{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}} struct {
    tflint.DefaultRule
}

func New{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}() *{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}} {
    return &{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}{}
}

func (r *{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}) Name() string {
    return "{{COMPANY_SLUG}}_my_rule_name"
}

func (r *{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}) Enabled() bool { return true }

func (r *{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}) Severity() tflint.Severity {
    return tflint.{{SEVERITY}}  // ERROR, WARNING, NOTICE
}

func (r *{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}) Link() string {
    return "{{DOCS_URL}}/rules/{{COMPANY_SLUG}}_my_rule_name"
}

func (r *{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}) Check(runner tflint.Runner) error {
    {{CHECK_LOGIC}}
    return nil
}
```

## Enabling Rules in `.tflint.hcl`

```hcl
plugin "{{COMPANY_SLUG}}" {
  enabled = true
  version = "{{TFLINT_PLUGIN_VERSION}}"
  source  = "{{TFLINT_PLUGIN_SOURCE}}"
}

rule "{{COMPANY_SLUG}}_my_rule_name" {
  enabled = true
}
```

## Severity Guidelines
| Level | When to Use |
|-------|-------------|
| `ERROR` | Blocks CI — naming violations, banned resources |
| `WARNING` | Should fix — non-standard patterns, missing recommended args |
| `NOTICE` | Informational — stylistic suggestions |

## Running tflint
```bash
# Install plugins and run
tflint --init
tflint --recursive

# Run on a single module directory
tflint --chdir=./modules/{{MODULE_NAME}}
```

## Rule Test Boilerplate

```go
package rules

import (
    "testing"

    "github.com/terraform-linters/tflint-plugin-sdk/helper"
)

func TestCheck{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}(t *testing.T) {
    tests := []struct {
        name     string
        config   string
        expected []helper.Issue
    }{
        {
            name: "valid — no issues",
            config: `
resource "{{TERRAFORM_RESOURCE_TYPE}}" "default" {
    {{VALID_CONFIG}}
}`,
            expected: []helper.Issue{},
        },
        {
            name: "invalid — rule violation",
            config: `
resource "{{TERRAFORM_RESOURCE_TYPE}}" "default" {
    {{INVALID_CONFIG}}
}`,
            expected: []helper.Issue{
                {Rule: New{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}(), Message: "{{EXPECTED_ERROR_MESSAGE}}"},
            },
        },
    }

    for _, tt := range tests {
        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            runner := helper.TestRunner()
            runner.AddContent("main.tf", tt.config)
            if err := New{{RULE_STRUCT_NAME}}().Check(runner); err != nil {
                t.Fatal(err)
            }
            helper.AssertIssues(t, tt.expected, runner.Issues)
        })
    }
}
```
